Key Takeaway

Azure Load Balancer is a highly available Layer 4 networking service that distributes TCP and UDP traffic across multiple backend resources. By using frontend configurations, backend pools, health probes, and load balancing rules, Azure Administrators can build scalable, resilient applications that remain available even when individual servers fail. For AZ-104, understanding load balancer components, public versus internal deployments, health probes, and Standard versus Basic SKUs is essential.
